7. B1.3 – Improve the Search Order (2 Marks)
We implemented two versions to improve the search process.

Version 1: Original Input Order
- Vertices are selected in their given order.
- No special selection rule is used.
- It provides the baseline performance.
Version 2: Highest Degree First

Our selection rule is:
1. Calculate the degree of every vertex.
2. Select the vertex with the highest degree first.
3. Continue with the remaining vertices in descending degree order.
4. If two vertices have equal degree, select the smaller vertex number first.
Why did we choose this rule?

Highly connected vertices have more restrictions on their colour choices. Selecting them first can expose conflicts earlier and reduce unnecessary searching.
