10. Time and Space Complexity
Let:
- \(V\) = Number of vertices.
- \(M\) = Number of available colours.
- \(E\) = Number of edges.
Complexity	Value
Worst-case time	\(O(M^V \times (V+E))\)
Space	\(O(V+E)\)

The algorithm may explore up to \(M^V\) possible colour assignments in the worst case.
